From ec1d46fa1fc81b774fffa26a33d139c51b93046f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yago Lasse <yagolasse@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 01:19:43 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: name host threads (SetThreadDescription)

Profilers and debuggers only saw start addresses: every guest thread starts
in the same bridge trampoline, and the nearest PDB symbol of a host thread's
start is often unrelated. Add a header-only xbox_name_thread() (include/xbox/
thread_name.h; SetThreadDescription looked up at run time, a no-op without
it) and name the threads at creation: guest threads as
"guest #<n> <routine>(<ctx1>)" (XAPI passes the title's routine as ctx1),
the main guest thread in INLINE mode too, and the runtime's own threads
(nv2a ack/pushbuffer, watchdog, watch resolver, kernel timers, sw raster N,
ohci usb, fb window, video pump, and the APU shim's qemu threads by name).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ahYm8JBvCH5KhgtSu9Yoy
